"text":"Ordered to special consent calendar.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-passed","code":null,"date":"2026-08-20","eventType":"passed_house","historyId":"119112598","location":"Senate","sequence":20,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Read third time. Passed. Ordered to the Assembly. (Ayes 39. Noes 0. Page 5589.).","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-other","code":null,"date":"2026-08-20","eventType":"legislative_action","historyId":"119112600","location":"Assembly","sequence":21,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"In Assembly. Ordered to Engrossing and Enrolling.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-enrolled","code":null,"date":"2026-08-27","eventType":"enrolled","historyId":"119112602","location":"Governor","sequence":22,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Enrolled and presented to the Governor at 4 p.m.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-approved","code":null,"date":"2026-09-27","eventType":"approved_by_governor","historyId":"119112604","location":"Governor","sequence":23,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Approved by the Governor.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-chaptered","code":null,"date":"2026-09-27","eventType":"chaptered","historyId":"119112606","location":"Secretary of State","sequence":24,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Chaptered by Secretary of State - Chapter 532, Statutes of 2026.","time":null,"votes":[]}],"affectedStatutes":[{"action":"IS_AMENDED","code":"ELEC","text":"Section 2225 of the Elections Code is amended to read:"}],"approvedDate":"2026-09-27","chapter":{"citation":"Chapter 532, Statutes of 2026","number":"532","type":"CHP","year":"2026"},"chapteredDate":"2026-09-27","committees":[],"conditions":[],"contentHash":"a20424c375bf5a9f598248f9df03e0b131cef719892c7cdb2b47bd78dc9c53c3","cosponsorCount":null,"digest":"Existing law requires a county elections official to take various actions to confirm voters’ residency, including by, among other things, mailing a postcard to each registered voter of the county or obtaining change-of-address data from the United States Postal Service. If the postcard is returned by the post office as undeliverable and the voter has no forwarding address, or if the change-of-address data indicates that the voter has moved and left no forwarding address, existing law requires the county elections official to update the voter’s registration status to inactive and mail notice to the voter of that change.\n\nThis bill would require a county elections official to take the following additional steps to provide notice to a voter when United States Postal Service data indicates a voter has a mailing address that is different from the voter’s residence address and the mailing address is no longer valid: 1) if a new mailing address is available via change-of-address data, the elections official would be required to update the voter’s registration record with the new mailing address and send a forwardable notice to the new address to confirm the change; 2) if a new mailing address is not identified and the voter can receive mail at their physical residence, the elections official would be required to send notice to the voter’s physical residence and remove the invalid mailing address from the record; or, 3) if a new mailing address is not identified and the voter cannot receive mail at their physical residence, the elections official would be required to send a specified notice to the voter’s mailing address on the voter’s registration record.\n\nBy increasing the duties of county elections officials, this bill would impose a state-mandated local program.\n\nThe California Constitution requires the state to reimburse local agencies and school districts for certain costs mandated by the state. Statutory provisions establish procedures for making that reimbursement.\n\nThis bill would provide that, if the Commission on State Mandates determines that the bill contains costs mandated by the state, reimbursement for those costs shall be made pursuant to the statutory provisions noted above.","digestDate":null,"digestVersion":null,"effective":{"basis":"not_verified","date":null,"note":"No effective date is recorded in the official bill data and DemocracyHQ has not verified one. A non-urgency statute enacted in a regular session generally takes effect on January 1 after a 90-day period (Cal. Const. art. IV, § 8(c)), but a bill may state other operative dates."},"expiryClauses":[],"firstObservedAt":"2026-11-20T01:12:59Z","id":"ca-20252026-ab1610","identifier":"AB 1610","indicators":{"Appropriation":"NO","BudgetBill":"NO","Election":"NO","FiscalCommittee":"YES","ImmediateEffect":"NO","LocalProgram":"YES","TaxLevy":"NO","Urgency":"NO","UsualCurrentExpenses":"NO","VoteRequired":"MAJORITY"},"introducedDate":"2026-01-20","issueTags":[{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"Legislative Counsel's digest","matchedText":"would be required to update the voter’s registration record with the new mailing address and send a","ruleId":"tag-reg-1","tag":"registration"}],"judicialNote":"Legislative status does not show whether a court has blocked, narrowed or upheld any provision. Check the linked litigation, which may be incomplete.","lastActionDate":"2026-09-27","lastActionText":"Chaptered by Secretary of State - Chapter 532, Statutes of 2026.","lastCheckedAt":"2026-11-21T09:01:56Z","leadAuthors":"Introduced by Assembly Member Ransom","legislativeStatus":{"currentHouse":"Secretary of State","currentLocation":null,"currentStatus":"Chaptered","measureState":"Chaptered"},"legislativeSubjects":[],"measureType":"Assembly Bill","officialUrl":"https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billNavClient.xhtml?bill_id=202520260AB1610","policyArea":null,"relatedMeasures":[],"selection":{"matchedField":"official subject line (latest version)","matchedText":"Elections","ruleId":"ca-select-2"